  "goodToKnow": "Akademisch means academic: ein akademischer Grad, die akademische Welt. In German, der Akademiker is anyone with a university degree, not only a researcher. A university tradition is das akademische Viertel: lectures marked c.t. (cum tempore) start 15 minutes after the hour, while s.t. (sine tempore) means sharp. Eine rein akademische Frage is purely theoretical. From Plato's Akademie in Athens."
